HEADIF:place;bsd
TEXT

The @code{place} is like an @code{include}, but the contents
of the file is not recurrently scanned for macros.

To have the @code{builtin} not to recurrently scan the output
the setting thereof is overruled with the @code{recur_n}.

END
CODE
0_define:\Bplace(;;include;nr11 ;m4;;;m4exec
0_define:place;;include;nn00;m4;;recur_n;m4builtin
END
